`lowPrefix = (BYTE*)dest`, `dictStart = dict`, `dictSize = 64*1024 - 1`.

Now, `checkOffset = (safeDecode) && (dictSize < (int)(64 KB))`. `dictSize = 65535`, `64 KB = 65536`. So `dictSize < 64 KB` is true, and `checkOffset = 1`.

The check `match + dictSize < lowPrefix` becomes `match + 65535 < dest`. If `match >= dest - 65535`, the check passes.

But `match = op - offset`. If `offset > op - (dest - 65535) = (op - dest) + 65535`, then `match < dest - 65535`, and it errors.

If `offset <= (op - dest) + 65535`, then `match >= dest - 65535`, and the check passes.

Then `if ((dict==usingExtDict) && (match < lowPrefix))` - if `match < dest`, it enters the dictionary match copy code.

`copySize = lowPrefix - match = dest - match`. Since `match >= dest - 65535`, `copySize <= 65535 = dictSize`. And `dictEnd - copySize = (dict + 65535) - copySize >= dict`. So the dictionary read is within bounds.

